WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:04.540
An early Christian principle
says: what Christ did not take on,

2
00:00:04.590 --> 00:00:06.180
he did not heal.

3
00:00:06.230 --> 00:00:09.850
Christians believe Christ
came to save all people.

4
00:00:09.900 --> 00:00:11.650
But Christ was a man.

5
00:00:11.700 --> 00:00:16.700
For centuries, Christ's maleness
was used to rank men above women.

6
00:00:16.750 --> 00:00:20.710
If his maleness is what
saves, women seem left out.

7
00:00:20.760 --> 00:00:23.930
So can a male saviour save women?

8
00:00:23.980 --> 00:00:26.770
In this mission, you'll meet
Rosemary Radford Ruether,

9
00:00:26.820 --> 00:00:31.070
a theologian who put this very
question at the heart of her book.

10
00:00:31.120 --> 00:00:33.180
Then you'll weigh up how other Christians,

11
00:00:33.230 --> 00:00:36.440
and other feminists,
responded to her answer.

12
00:00:36.490 --> 00:00:40.220
Your mission: find out how
Christians answer the question:

13
00:00:40.270 --> 00:00:42.610
can a male saviour save women?
